00:46:52,940 --> 00:46:59,940
So, here is the hyperbola for stocks and bonds.

1088
00:46:59,940 --> 00:47:01,940
So, just as I had a

1089
00:47:01,940 --> 00:47:03,940
point here, which represented 100% VOC,

1090
00:47:03,940 --> 00:47:06,940
I can have over here a

1091
00:47:06,940 --> 00:47:09,940
point, which represents 100% U.S. stocks.

1092
00:47:09,940 --> 00:47:10,940
Okay?

1093
00:47:10,940 --> 00:47:13,440
And I can take another point,

1094
00:47:13,440 --> 00:47:15,940
which is 100% bonds, that's here.

1095
00:47:15,940 --> 00:47:19,940
This point is 25% stocks, 75% bonds.

1096
00:47:19,940 --> 00:47:22,940
This point is 50% stocks, 50% bonds.

1097
00:47:22,940 --> 00:47:23,940
Okay?

1098
00:47:23,940 --> 00:47:27,440
And I can see that this is the choice set

1099
00:47:27,440 --> 00:47:30,940
that I, as an investor, have between stocks and bonds.

1100
00:47:30,940 --> 00:47:31,940
Okay?

1101
00:47:31,940 --> 00:47:34,940
So, is that clear?

1102
00:47:34,940 --> 00:47:38,940
Is that any?

1103
00:47:38,940 --> 00:47:40,440
So, again, there's no, you

1104
00:47:40,440 --> 00:47:41,940
see, all these are different portfolios.

1105
00:47:41,940 --> 00:47:46,440
If you're just going to do stocks and bonds and nothing else,

1106
00:47:46,440 --> 00:47:50,940
what you choose to do depends on your taste, on your risk tolerance.

1107
00:47:50,940 --> 00:47:52,940
I could go 100% stocks, but I'm

1108
00:47:52,940 --> 00:47:54,940
going to have a lot of risk.

1109
00:47:54,940 --> 00:47:57,940
I'm going to have a nice expected return.

1110
00:47:57,940 --> 00:48:00,940
It looks like it's about 13%, 14%.

1111
00:48:00,940 --> 00:48:02,940
But I'm going to have a high variance.

1112
00:48:02,940 --> 00:48:05,940
It looks like it's about 18%.

1113
00:48:05,940 --> 00:48:08,940
This is the S&P 500 stock market.

1114
00:48:08,940 --> 00:48:11,940
And so, it has a lot of variance.

1115
00:48:11,940 --> 00:48:13,440
I could be safe and

1116
00:48:13,440 --> 00:48:14,940
I could go all in bonds.

1117
00:48:14,940 --> 00:48:16,940
I could be here.

1118
00:48:16,940 --> 00:48:18,940
Then I'd have, you know, a lower, much

1119
00:48:18,940 --> 00:48:20,940
lower return, but I have a lower variance.

1120
00:48:20,940 --> 00:48:22,940
So, what should I do?

1121
00:48:22,940 --> 00:48:24,940
Well, what do you learn from this?

1122
00:48:24,940 --> 00:48:26,940
First of all, you learn

1123
00:48:26,940 --> 00:48:28,940
there isn't any single optimal portfolio.

1124
00:48:28,940 --> 00:48:29,940
But, you know, you can do it.

1125
00:48:29,940 --> 00:48:30,940
You can do it.

1126
00:48:30,940 --> 00:48:31,940
You can do it.

1127
00:48:31,940 --> 00:48:34,940
But there is something.

1128
00:48:34,940 --> 00:48:37,940
Let's talk about being a 100% bond investor.

1129
00:48:37,940 --> 00:48:38,940
What do you think of that?

1130
00:48:38,940 --> 00:48:40,940
Is that a good idea?

1131
00:48:40,940 --> 00:48:44,940
You'd get this point right here.

1132
00:48:44,940 --> 00:48:49,940
Well, you definitely should not be a 100% bond investor.

1133
00:48:49,940 --> 00:48:51,940
That's one thing we just learned.

1134
00:48:51,940 --> 00:48:52,940
Why is that?

1135
00:48:52,940 --> 00:48:56,940
Because if I go up here, I have no more.

1136
00:48:56,940 --> 00:48:59,940
See, that's the same standard deviation, the same risk.

1137
00:48:59,940 --> 00:49:03,940
I have a higher return.

1138
00:49:03,940 --> 00:49:04,940
Right?

1139
00:49:04,940 --> 00:49:07,940
Higher expected return.

1140
00:49:07,940 --> 00:49:08,940
So, what did we just learn?

1141
00:49:08,940 --> 00:49:10,940
We learned that if you just stay in this

1142
00:49:10,940 --> 00:49:12,940
space of stocks and bonds, maybe you could be a

1143
00:49:12,940 --> 00:49:15,940
100% stock investor, but never in a million

1144
00:49:15,940 --> 00:49:18,940
years should you ever even think of being

1145
00:49:18,940 --> 00:49:19,940
a 100% bond investor.

1146
00:49:19,940 --> 00:49:20,940
Okay?

1147
00:49:20,940 --> 00:49:23,940
Because, look, it's just simple math.

1148
00:49:23,940 --> 00:49:24,940
I can figure it out.

1149
00:49:24,940 --> 00:49:26,940
I can figure out that I get

1150
00:49:26,940 --> 00:49:28,940
a higher expected return and no more risk.

1151
00:49:28,940 --> 00:49:32,940
So, this is lesson number one that Markowitz showed us.

1152
00:49:32,940 --> 00:49:33,940
Amazing.

1153
00:49:33,940 --> 00:49:35,940
It's so simple and obvious, right?

1154
00:49:35,940 --> 00:49:39,440
It's not so simple, because at the time

1155
00:49:39,440 --> 00:49:42,940
Markowitz wrote, Yale University was probably a 100%

1156
00:49:42,940 --> 00:49:45,940
bond investor, believe it or not.

1157
00:49:45,940 --> 00:49:47,940
They couldn't figure it out in those days.

1158
00:49:47,940 --> 00:49:51,940
So, we've made progress.

1159
00:49:51,940 --> 00:49:54,940
That's why I think Markowitz is among the

1160
00:49:54,940 --> 00:49:57,940
most deserving of the Nobel Prize winners in economics.

1161
00:49:57,940 --> 00:49:59,940
This is really basic.

1162
00:49:59,940 --> 00:50:01,940
It actually intrigues me.

1163
00:50:01,940 --> 00:50:04,440
I don't know how much you like math, but

1164
00:50:04,440 --> 00:50:06,940
going back to my childhood, I was interested in geometry.

1165
00:50:06,940 --> 00:50:11,940
These simple mathematical curiosities like

1166
00:50:11,940 --> 00:50:16,940
hyperbola are just fascinating to me.

1167
00:50:16,940 --> 00:50:21,440
It goes back to Apollonius of Perga, writing in

1168
00:50:21,440 --> 00:50:25,940
around 200 BC, wrote a book on conic sections.

1169
00:50:25,940 --> 00:50:27,940
And he wrote,

1170
00:50:27,940 --> 00:50:33,940
he invented the word hyperbola, parabola, ellipse.

1171
00:50:33,940 --> 00:50:36,940
So, I was thinking of looking back at his book, I

1172
00:50:36,940 --> 00:50:39,940
think it still survives, and seeing what he says about finance.

1173
00:50:39,940 --> 00:50:42,440
But I can be sure, he had no

1174
00:50:42,440 --> 00:50:44,940
idea that his theory would apply to finance.

1175
00:50:44,940 --> 00:50:46,440
I wish I could go back in

1176
00:50:46,440 --> 00:50:47,940
a time machine and talk to him.

1177
00:50:47,940 --> 00:50:52,440
He would be so happy to know that his theory of conic

1178
00:50:52,440 --> 00:50:56,940
sections, you know, it ended up applied to astronomy by Kepler and Newton.

1179
00:50:56,940 --> 00:50:58,940
And now it hits into finance.

1180
00:50:58,940 --> 00:51:02,940
Isn't it amazing how there's a unity of thought?

1181
00:51:02,940 --> 00:51:04,940
And this simple diagram has

1182
00:51:04,940 --> 00:51:06,940
just taught us something about investing.

1183
00:51:06,940 --> 00:51:08,940
That's not obvious.

1184
00:51:08,940 --> 00:51:11,940
Not obvious until you think about it.

1185
00:51:11,940 --> 00:51:16,940
I've just told you, never invest only in bonds.

1186
00:51:16,940 --> 00:51:20,940
But it doesn't tell you how much stocks and

1187
00:51:20,940 --> 00:51:24,940
how much bonds to, once you're above this point,

1188
00:51:24,940 --> 00:51:26,940
it seems to be a matter of taste.

1189
00:51:26,940 --> 00:51:32,940
It isn't any single decision that you can make.

1190
00:51:32,940 --> 00:51:36,940
So, now I want to move to a

1191
00:51:36,940 --> 00:51:40,940
more complicated world, where we have three assets.

1192
00:51:40,940 --> 00:51:41,940
Okay.

1193
00:51:41,940 --> 00:51:43,940
We're starting from, we had one

1194
00:51:43,940 --> 00:51:45,940
risky asset, then we had two.

1195
00:51:45,940 --> 00:51:47,940
Now, let's go even further.

1196
00:51:47,940 --> 00:51:50,940
Let's say three risky assets.

1197
00:51:50,940 --> 00:51:55,940
Well, the expected return is the same.

1198
00:51:55,940 --> 00:51:56,940
It's the weighted average.

1199
00:51:56,940 --> 00:51:58,940
Now, we have three weights.

1200
00:51:58,940 --> 00:52:01,940
X1, X2, and X3.

1201
00:52:01,940 --> 00:52:03,940
And they have to sum to one dollar.

1202
00:52:03,940 --> 00:52:05,940
I could have written X3

1203
00:52:05,940 --> 00:52:07,940
as 1 minus X1 minus X2.

1204
00:52:07,940 --> 00:52:09,940
I wrote it differently here.

1205
00:52:09,940 --> 00:52:12,940
It looked messy to write it the other way.

1206
00:52:12,940 --> 00:52:15,940
And this is the formula for the portfolio variance.

1207
00:52:15,940 --> 00:52:18,440
It's the X1 squared times the variance

1208
00:52:18,440 --> 00:52:20,940
of the return on the first risky asset,

1209
00:52:20,940 --> 00:52:22,940
plus X2 squared times the variance of

1210
00:52:22,940 --> 00:52:24,940
the return on the second risky asset,

1211
00:52:24,940 --> 00:52:25,440
plus X3 squared times the variance of

1212
00:52:25,440 --> 00:52:25,940
the return on the second risky asset,

1213
00:52:25,940 --> 00:52:27,940
plus X2 squared times the variance of

1214
00:52:27,940 --> 00:52:29,940
the return on the third risky asset.

1215
00:52:29,940 --> 00:52:33,940
And then you have three more terms representing covariances.

1216
00:52:33,940 --> 00:52:35,440
You have to take account

1217
00:52:35,440 --> 00:52:36,940
of the covariances of the asset,

1218
00:52:36,940 --> 00:52:39,440
because if they move together, if they all

1219
00:52:39,440 --> 00:52:41,940
go in the same direction at the same time,

1220
00:52:41,940 --> 00:52:45,940
that's going to make your portfolio riskier.

1221
00:52:45,940 --> 00:52:48,940
And so, that's the portfolio variance.

1222
00:52:48,940 --> 00:52:50,940
And the portfolio expected return is

1223
00:52:50,940 --> 00:52:52,940
just, why didn't I write it there?

1224
00:52:52,940 --> 00:52:54,940
It's X1 R1 plus X2 R2 plus X3 R2.

1225
00:52:54,940 --> 00:53:01,940
Where the sum of the X's is 1, $1.

1226
00:53:01,940 --> 00:53:05,940
So, it's something that you can do

1227
00:53:05,940 --> 00:53:09,940
to calculate what is the optimal portfolio.

1228
00:53:09,940 --> 00:53:11,940
So, I decided to add

1229
00:53:11,940 --> 00:53:13,940
a third asset to my diagram.

1230
00:53:13,940 --> 00:53:17,440
The pink line up here is the

1231
00:53:17,440 --> 00:53:20,940
same, we call that an efficient portfolio frontier.

1232
00:53:20,940 --> 00:53:22,940
I have that in the title of the slide.

1233
00:53:23,940 --> 00:53:25,940
For stocks and bonds.

1234
00:53:25,940 --> 00:53:27,940
That's the pink line here.

1235
00:53:27,940 --> 00:53:31,940
But I've added the efficient portfolio

1236
00:53:31,940 --> 00:53:35,940
frontier for three stocks, three assets.

1237
00:53:35,940 --> 00:53:38,940
Stocks, bonds, and oil.

1238
00:53:38,940 --> 00:53:42,440
Oil is an important investment,

1239
00:53:42,440 --> 00:53:45,940
because our economy runs on it.

1240
00:53:45,940 --> 00:53:48,440
And the total value of oil in the ground is

1241
00:53:48,440 --> 00:53:50,940
comparable to the value of the stock markets of the world.

1242
00:53:50,940 --> 00:53:52,940
So, it's big and important.

1243
00:53:52,940 --> 00:53:56,940
So, let's put that in.

1244
00:53:56,940 --> 00:54:04,440
And what I have actually here is the minimum variance

1245
00:54:04,440 --> 00:54:11,940
mixture for any given return, expected return for the three assets.

1246
00:54:11,940 --> 00:54:16,940
And you can see that it's possible when you add a

1247
00:54:16,940 --> 00:54:21,940
third asset, oil, to bring the efficient portfolio frontier to the left.

1248
00:54:22,940 --> 00:54:26,440
And that's not the problem, because we've got

1249
00:54:26,440 --> 00:54:29,940
another asset, and it's also paying a good return.

1250
00:54:29,940 --> 00:54:31,940
And it's not correlated very much.

1251
00:54:31,940 --> 00:54:34,940
Oil doesn't correlate very much with the stock market.

1252
00:54:34,940 --> 00:54:38,940
So, we're spreading the risk out over more assets.

1253
00:54:38,940 --> 00:54:42,940
We're putting more eggs in our basket.

1254
00:54:42,940 --> 00:54:44,940
Okay.

1255
00:54:44,940 --> 00:54:47,940
And so, then we are,

1256
00:54:47,940 --> 00:54:50,940
we have a better, a better.

1257
00:54:50,940 --> 00:54:51,940
Yeah.

1258
00:54:51,940 --> 00:54:54,940
A better choice set now, right?

1259
00:54:54,940 --> 00:54:57,940
We can pick any point on that blue line.

1260
00:54:57,940 --> 00:55:00,940
And so, we shouldn't just have stocks and bonds.

1261
00:55:00,940 --> 00:55:04,940
We've learned we should have stocks, bonds, and oil.

1262
00:55:04,940 --> 00:55:08,940
We're lending, we're leading toward a fundamental insight, which

1263
00:55:08,940 --> 00:55:12,940
is due to Markowitz, which is, the more the merrier.

1264
00:55:12,940 --> 00:55:16,440
The more different kinds of assets you can put in, the lower

1265
00:55:16,440 --> 00:55:19,940
you can get the standard deviation of your return for any given interest.

1266
00:55:19,940 --> 00:55:20,940
Okay.

1267
00:55:21,940 --> 00:55:24,440
And so, the more you can get the standard

1268
00:55:24,440 --> 00:55:26,940
deviation of your return for any given expected return.

1269
00:55:26,940 --> 00:55:28,940
And so, the better off you are.

1270
00:55:28,940 --> 00:55:30,940
So, this is diversification.

1271
00:55:30,940 --> 00:55:35,440
So, while diversification was applauded in the 19th century,

1272
00:55:35,440 --> 00:55:39,940
no one had ever done the math like this before.

1273
00:55:39,940 --> 00:55:43,440
And now, we can see that you, when you do

1274
00:55:43,440 --> 00:55:46,940
the math, you want to have all three in your portfolio.

1275
00:55:46,940 --> 00:55:48,940
And yet, people don't know that.

1276
00:55:48,940 --> 00:55:49,940
They don't.

1277
00:55:49,940 --> 00:55:53,940
And so, there's an emotional resistance to this implication.

1278
00:55:53,940 --> 00:55:59,940
I once went to the government of Norway, gave a talk

1279
00:55:59,940 --> 00:56:05,940
at their Norges Bank, which is the central bank of Norway.

1280
00:56:05,940 --> 00:56:10,440
And I told them in my talk, I calculate that

1281
00:56:10,440 --> 00:56:14,940
Norway has something like 70% of its portfolio in oil.

1282
00:56:14,940 --> 00:56:16,440
I don't remember the exact number,

1283
00:56:16,440 --> 00:56:17,940
but it was something close to that.

1284
00:56:17,940 --> 00:56:19,940
Why do they have so much in oil?

1285
00:56:19,940 --> 00:56:22,940
Well, because they have the North Sea oil.

1286
00:56:22,940 --> 00:56:27,440
And so, I asked them at the bank,

1287
00:56:27,440 --> 00:56:31,940
don't you realize, where are you on this portfolio?

1288
00:56:31,940 --> 00:56:33,940
You're not on the frontier.

1289
00:56:33,940 --> 00:56:37,940
What Norway should be doing is something like 15%.

1290
00:56:37,940 --> 00:56:38,940
They could pick this point, right?

1291
00:56:38,940 --> 00:56:39,940
That would be reasonable.

1292
00:56:39,940 --> 00:56:42,940
15% oil, 53% stocks, 32% bonds,

1293
00:56:42,940 --> 00:56:45,940
which would give them that point.

1294
00:56:45,940 --> 00:56:48,940
Or they could pick this one.

1295
00:56:48,940 --> 00:56:49,940
I have a point labeled up here.

1296
00:56:49,940 --> 00:56:54,940
That's 21% oil, 79% stocks, no bonds.

1297
00:56:54,940 --> 00:56:55,940
All right?

1298
00:56:55,940 --> 00:56:57,940
Those are all choices, depending on your risk.

1299
00:56:57,940 --> 00:57:00,940
But they're not going to just pick 100% oil.

1300
00:57:00,940 --> 00:57:05,940
That would be way over here, much higher risk.

1301
00:57:05,940 --> 00:57:07,940
So, I asked them about that.

1302
00:57:07,940 --> 00:57:09,940
Why do you do this?

1303
00:57:09,940 --> 00:57:13,440
And I don't know if I got a good answer from them,

1304
00:57:13,440 --> 00:57:16,940
but basically, it was, well, we don't want to sell the oil,

1305
00:57:16,940 --> 00:57:17,940
because it's our national oil.

1306
00:57:17,940 --> 00:57:19,440
We don't want to sell

1307
00:57:19,440 --> 00:57:20,940
it because it's our national heritage.

1308
00:57:20,940 --> 00:57:21,940
We own it.

1309
00:57:21,940 --> 00:57:23,940
And I said, well, you don't have to sell it.

1310
00:57:23,940 --> 00:57:25,940
You can just do a derivative transaction.

1311
00:57:25,940 --> 00:57:27,940
You can short the futures market

1312
00:57:27,940 --> 00:57:29,940
for oil and reduce your exposure.

1313
00:57:29,940 --> 00:57:32,940
And then they said, well, some people

1314
00:57:32,940 --> 00:57:35,940
have mentioned that, but it's politically difficult.

1315
00:57:35,940 --> 00:57:37,940
So, they're not doing it.

1316
00:57:37,940 --> 00:57:42,940
Maybe next year, maybe the next government will do that.

1317
00:57:42,940 --> 00:57:44,940
So, they still aren't there yet.

1318
00:57:44,940 --> 00:57:46,940
They're not managing their risks well.

1319
00:57:46,940 --> 00:57:48,940
But it's a powerful and important thing.

1320
00:57:48,940 --> 00:57:51,940
Because if the market for oil

1321
00:57:51,940 --> 00:57:54,940
collapses, Norway is in big trouble.

1322
00:57:54,940 --> 00:57:57,940
They're not diversifying enough.

1323
00:57:57,940 --> 00:57:59,940
I don't mean to put them down.

1324
00:57:59,940 --> 00:58:00,940
They're smart people.

1325
00:58:00,940 --> 00:58:02,440
But like in any country, I

1326
00:58:02,440 --> 00:58:03,940
did the same thing with Mexico.

1327
00:58:03,940 --> 00:58:06,940
I went to the Banco de Mexico, and I

1328
00:58:06,940 --> 00:58:09,940
talked to Guillermo Ortiz, when he was director of it.

1329
00:58:09,940 --> 00:58:10,940
Same thing.

1330
00:58:10,940 --> 00:58:14,940
Mexico is not as dependent on oil as Norway is.

1331
00:58:14,940 --> 00:58:15,940
But it's a big problem.

1332
00:58:15,940 --> 00:58:22,940
I think, it's not so obvious for Mexico.

1333
00:58:22,940 --> 00:58:24,940
But it is politics that came in.

1334
00:58:24,940 --> 00:58:29,940
The question of, are you really saying Mexico should go into the futures

1335
00:58:29,940 --> 00:58:34,940
market and take a massive short position of billions of dollars of oil?

1336
00:58:34,940 --> 00:58:37,940
Again, it was like, this isn't reality.

1337
00:58:37,940 --> 00:58:39,940
We're not going to do that.

1338
00:58:39,940 --> 00:58:44,940
But I tried to make the point.

1339
00:58:45,940 --> 00:58:47,940
I think, it's a big problem.

1340
00:58:47,940 --> 00:58:49,940
Now, another thing is, so

1341
00:58:49,940 --> 00:58:51,940
I have shown here three assets.

1342
00:58:51,940 --> 00:58:53,940
